From 12b45ebaac007f883060fae2bd76e8f4eebba0f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 06:23:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] mav: refuse reboot, param reset and calibration while
 armed

Three commands did something dangerous to an armed vehicle and were
accepted without looking at the arm state:
  * PREFLIGHT_REBOOT_SHUTDOWN (p1 1/3): ESP.restart() mid-water drops every
    thruster and comes back disarmed in MANUAL at an unknown depth.
  * PREFLIGHT_STORAGE p1=2: the reset is live - every gain, FRAME_REVERSE
    (=1 on this hull, so every axis inverts in one step) and each MOT_n_DIR
    plus the learned motor directions change under a running controller.
  * PREFLIGHT_CALIBRATION (all sub-types): BARO_ZERO at depth makes that
    depth "0 m", so the failsafe's surface-then-disarm disarms AT DEPTH;
    gyro/level cal averages the vehicle's own motion into the offsets.

Each now goes through disarmedGate(): proceed only when positively known
disarmed; otherwise MAV_RESULT_TEMPORARILY_REJECTED (terminal ACK) plus a
STATUSTEXT "<what> refused: disarm first" ("state busy" on a lock miss,
which refuses rather than guessing). PREFLIGHT_STORAGE p1=1 (save) stays
allowed - it changes nothing live.

Crosses the companion contract (behaviour, not wire constants):
JETSON_COMMS.md updated. mongla_ws's calibrate_depth already gates on
disarmed, so its normal path is unaffected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KchLnXUAMJ6S4pj3BZLobN
